<msg type="info" file="MapLib" num="355" delta="unknown" >SelectRam <arg fmt="%s" index="1">RAM16X1S symbol &quot;inst_Mram_mem10&quot; (output signal=ram/_varindex0000&lt;0&gt;)</arg> INITSTATE is changed from <arg fmt="%s" index="2">007F</arg> to <arg fmt="%s" index="3">7f7f</arg> because pin <arg fmt="%s" index="4">A3 </arg> is/are driven by GND. Signals driving <arg fmt="%s" index="5">A3 </arg> are inverted to relieve routing congestion.
